# Native Components Rules

Do not import, register, or use Syncfusion `@syncfusion/*` packages or `<ejs-*>` tags. Use the native `vxceed*` / `Native*` components already in this repo.

## Hard rules

- Never add `@syncfusion/*` dependencies or `from '@syncfusion/...'` imports.
- Never introduce new `<ejs-*>` tags.
- Prefer existing `vxceed*` / `Native*` components over a new third-party UI kit.
- `.e-*` and `mfc-ejs-*` class names on native components are CSS compatibility only. Do not restore Syncfusion to “match” them.
- Vue 3 Options API remains mandatory for app components unless explicitly requested otherwise.

## When editing legacy screens

- Replace remaining `<ejs-*>` usage with the map in `central-project-rules.mdc`.
- Do not add dual Syncfusion/native branches in new UI work.
